      "summaryMarkdown": "Full review at plan revision 5 (the stored review was cleared by the repair batch and CORE-2/CORE-3 changed, so no reattest). CORE-1: one `ServiceKey` space; runtime and type keys share descriptors, caches, resolution guards, scope and disposal paths; factory errors are not cached; typed behavior unchanged apart from a poisoned-lock or wrong-API resolve now naming its cause instead of `Missing`. CORE-2: thread-bound slots without `unsafe`; a wrong-thread resolve fails before touching the table; values are never dropped off their thread (drains run outside the `RefCell` borrow, the table drops with its thread); the API kind is checked before any factory runs or cached value is returned. CORE-3: factories are made (bounded by the default timeout under a timer) before ordering over both key kinds; per-service timeouts, concurrent layers, failures and timeouts all named. CORE-4: registration-key defaulting for every `add_startup_*` form, explicit keys kept. The four test groups prove each, including the new factory-timeout and wrong-API tests; my scratch probe confirmed the three repairs. The earlier findings f1-f3 are resolved. Residual, non-blocking: a scope whose descriptor snapshot predates the root re-registering a key as the other kind can read that kind's cached singleton as an opaque value (never the thread-bound value).",
