      "summaryMarkdown": "Passed. All five findings of the first review are resolved. I inspected the repair delta:\n\n- `theme_keys_view::a_bound_text_style_follows_its_tokens`: a `bind_text_style(text, text_style_keys!(typography::h3))` node shows desktop's h3 and then, on the same node, touch's after `Density::Touch.set()`, with desktop != touch asserted first.\n- The appearance test now binds `surfaces::APP` and asserts that Light != Dark before switching. Brand and Reset act on `APP`.\n- `FixtureCommands` runs on the fixture only. `check` exits 1 for a missing file, `write` 0, `check` 0, and `check` 1 after one value is edited. A density token aliasing the accent color raises a `CodegenError` naming `borders-tint`, and `write` exits 2.\n- `document()` now derives each token's owning modifier from `ROOTS` and stops on strays.\n- `theming.md:211`, components `knowledge.md` and `SKILL.md:131-135` are corrected.\n\nI reran the Python group (15 OK). `theme_codegen.py check` still reports `theme.json` current. The Rust groups' fresh passing results come from `check` at revision 39.\n\nThe first review's assessment of NSH-1 and THEME-1..4 stands: the pin, no old-theme API, no modifier set by RayX, Light/Dark outside the modifiers, Button token-for-token unchanged, and the document equal to the old dump in all 24 combinations.",
