      "descriptionMarkdown": "**Expected:** t24 moves the old groups' still-valid assertions into the new groups, and THEME-2 requires that a key read in a binding follows a modifier change. The old `theme_view` group asserted that `bind_text_style` follows a density switch: font size, line height and letter spacing on the same view.\n\n**Observed:** `bind_text_style` was rewritten onto `TextStyleKeys` (`crates/rayx_components/src/theme/mod.rs:305`, with the weight now an `untracked` snapshot), and `text_style_keys!` (`mod.rs:173`) is new. `theme_view` was deleted, and no test group calls either one: `grep -rn bind_text_style crates/rayx_components/tests examples/gallery/native` finds nothing. Only a `no_run` doctest compiles them. `Button` does not use them.\n\n**Failure scenario:** a regression in `bind_text_style` passes every sprint check. For example, a binding that reads the keys outside its closure would freeze the text style after `Density::Touch.set()`. Yet `docs/components.md`, `theming.md` and `SKILL.md` all present it as the way to apply a text style.\n\n**Repair:** add a case to `theme_keys_view` or `theme_modifiers_view`: a `bind_text_style(text(..), text_style_keys!(keys::platform::density::typography::h3))` view whose `text_styles` change from Desktop's to Touch's h3 values on the same node after `Density::Touch.set()`, with the expected values written as literals (as `button_view` does).",
